class:: FeatureDeltaDelta
summary:: Regression acceleration of a control feature
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Slope

description::
Applies the same HTK symmetric regression delta twice, once to feature values and once to the resulting deltas. The effective support is 4*N+1 updates and the group delay is 2*N updates.

A negative trigger accepts every control block. A nonnegative trigger accepts only positive edges and holds the output between edges; this lets the caller align updates with analysis frames. frameTime must match that regular update spacing. Irregular triggers do not create a nonuniform regression. Nonfinite input is replaced by zero. The first output appears after 4*radius+1 accepted values. Cost is O(radius) per accepted update and memory is fixed. Source: link::https://labrosa.ee.columbia.edu/doc/HTKBook21/node56.html::. Vanilla Slope is a one-step difference; regression uses a symmetric span of observations.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: in
Control-rate or scalar feature, with multichannel expansion for feature arrays.

argument:: radius
Literal symmetric regression radius from 1 through 32; total support is 2*radius+1 per regression pass.

argument:: trigger
Negative: update every control block. Otherwise update on positive edges.

argument:: frameTime
Seconds between accepted values. Zero uses the server control period; supply the actual period when triggering sparsely.

returns::
Second derivative in input units per second squared.

examples::
FeatureDeltaDelta computes the second regression derivative (acceleration) of a feature stream. In this example, energy acceleration isolates sudden strike transients in a drum loop: sharp bursts of acceleration spawn micro-granular dust resonance clusters, creating a percussive shadow. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.scope:: plots feature acceleration in real time.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("drums.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic drum fallback
            var trig = Impulse.kr(2);
            var kick = SinOsc.ar(EnvGen.ar(Env([120, 45], [0.08], \exp), trig)) * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.3), trig);
            var snare = WhiteNoise.ar * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.15), Impulse.kr(2, 0.5));
            (kick + snare) * 0.5
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var amp = Amplitude.kr(source, 0.002, 0.02);
        var accel = FeatureDeltaDelta.kr(amp, radius: 2, trigger: -1, frameTime: 0.01);
        var burstTrig = accel > 150;
        var grain = Ringz.ar(Dust2.ar(200 * burstTrig.lag(0.05)), 1200 + (accel.clip(0, 500) * 4), 0.02) * 0.2;
        var sound = (source * 0.25) + grain;

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, accel) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.scope("Energy Acceleration", ~mir2Bus, -200.0, 200.0, "1/s²");
});
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

